I think you're describing a glottal stop.  It's a sound that's similar
to [k] but in deed uttered further back in the mouth and throat, all the
way to glottis (=vocal cords).  I think that's present also in German,
perhaps in <Verein>, between the syllables Ver- + ein..?  It might be
much weaker, of course.  The glottal stop doesn't occur in every
English, though.

